efficiently Modeling Long Sequences with Structured State Spaces (S4) (Gu et al., 2022)
Method: Uses structured continuous-time state spaces to model long sequences.
Dataset: Long Range Arena (LRA) benchmark.
Advantages: Efficiently processes long sequences (10k+ steps).
Limitations: Parameters are fixed and cannot adapt dynamically to inputs.
Research Gap: Input-dependent state adjustment for chaotic spatial motion.
Possible Improvements: Upgrades to Mamba’s dynamic selection to handle erratic human player movements.
